# True Margin — Cursor Rules

## Context
Two-week overload-planning dashboard for Chatathon 2026 (WHOOP track).
React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS. No backend, no database, no live
integrations required for the demo.

## Rule Engine Is Not AI
The logic in src/logic/ruleEngine.ts must stay deterministic and fully
explainable in one sentence: if high-concentration task hours exceed
concentration-friendly open time, flag the day. Never replace this with an
ML model, embedding, or LLM call, and don't suggest doing so.

## Data Is Synthetic
Everything in src/logic/data.ts is synthetic demo data. Don't connect it to
a real calendar API, database, or auth provider. Keep the "SYNTHETIC"
comments intact when editing this file.

## Scope Discipline
Out of scope for this repo: user authentication, a database, a manager UI,
live calendar integration, live LLM calls for the delegation message. If a
request would require one of these, say so instead of building it.

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode, typed props and function signatures
- Tailwind CSS only, no additional CSS frameworks
- No animation libraries — the UI needs to read clearly on a projector
- Comment any synthetic, simulated, or mocked behavior inline

## Protect the Happy Path
Every change should leave `npm install && npm run dev` working and the core
flow intact: dashboard → flagged day → recommendation → accept. Flag any
change that risks breaking it before applying.
